---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import heroImage from '../assets/products/bamboo-scoop-matcha-composition-scaled.jpg';
import originsImage from '../assets/products/matcha-lifestyle2-scaled.jpg';
import sourcingImage from '../assets/journal/matcha-lifestyle3-scaled.jpg';

// Split into words at build time, so CSS can darken them one by one while scrolling.
const lead =
  'Kohaku exists because of a disappointing cup of matcha. Not offensively bad — worse than that. It tasted of nothing in particular: vaguely grassy, vaguely bitter, entirely anonymous. It had cost a great deal and told us nothing about where it came from.';
const leadWords = lead.split(' ');

const gardens = [
  {
    name: 'Uji, Kyoto',
    text: 'River fog settles in the valleys and acts as natural shade; the soil is heavy and mineral. Deep umami with a long vegetal sweetness and almost no edge. The flavour arrives slowly and stays.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Nishio, Aichi',
    text: 'Flat alluvial ground on the Yahagi river, which floods and enriches. Brighter and more forward than Uji — less of the low savoury depth, more immediate sweetness, a cleaner finish.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Yame, Fukuoka',
    text: 'Narrow mountain valleys with sharp swings between day and night temperature. Stressed plants concentrate, and this is the boldest of the three: mineral, structured, noticeably less sweet.',
  },
];
---

<!-- Text and sizes copied from the WordPress About page. -->
<BaseLayout title="About">
  <!-- The intro stays pinned (sticky) while the photo scrolls up over it; "Origins"
       then slides out from under the photo. Together the photo reads as a layer above both. -->
  <div class="stack">
  <div class="intro first-screen">
  <canvas class="dust" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>

  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Our story</p>
    <!-- Two beats: the second line rises more slowly than the first. -->
    <h1>
      <span class="line"><span>Nothing blended.</span></span>{' '}<span class="line slow"><span>Nothing hurried.</span></span>
    </h1>
    <p class="lead" style={`--n: ${leadWords.length}`}>
      {leadWords.map((word, i) => <span class="w" style={`--i: ${i}`}>{word + ' '}</span>)}
    </p>
  </section>
  </div>

  <!-- Scroll runway: the intro stays pinned while this passes, and the paragraph is "read" here. -->
  <div class="runway" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="wide-wrap">
    <Image
      class="wide"
      src={heroImage}
      alt="A white bowl of whisked matcha beside a bamboo chasen and a wooden scoop of powder"
      widths={[828, 1280, 1920]}
      sizes="100vw"
    />
  </div>
  </div>

  <section class="row first">
    <div>
      <h2>Origins</h2>
      <p>
        That bag turned out to be a blend, as most matcha sold outside Japan is. Leaf from several regions is combined
        to hold a flavour steady from one year to the next. It is a real craft, and there is nothing dishonest about it.
        But blending is designed to remove variation, and variation is the interesting part.
      </p>
      <p>
        What followed was two years of unglamorous research: drinking a great deal of tea, writing down what we noticed,
        and slowly working out that the differences we kept returning to were differences of place. Kohaku started
        properly in 2023, with one garden and far too much inventory.
      </p>
    </div>
    <Image
      src={originsImage}
      alt="Matcha powder, a black chawan and an iced matcha on a grey surface"
      widths={[480, 960]}
      sizes="(max-width: 781px) 88vw, 472px"
    />
  </section>

  <section class="row reverse">
    <Image
      src={sourcingImage}
      alt="A spoon of matcha powder beside a bowl and whisk, shot from above"
      widths={[480, 960]}
      sizes="(max-width: 781px) 88vw, 472px"
    />
    <div>
      <h2>Sourcing</h2>
      <p>We work with four growers across Uji, Nishio and Yame, and we buy from named gardens rather than from a broker’s blend.</p>
      <p>
        Shading is where matcha is decided. Three to four weeks before harvest the bushes are covered, cutting sunlight
        by as much as ninety percent. The plant responds by flooding its leaves with chlorophyll and amino acids, and that
        is where both the colour and the savoury depth come from. Shade too little and the tea is thin; shade too long and
        it goes flat.
      </p>
      <p>
        Only the first harvest goes into what we sell. Later flushes are cheaper, coarser and more astringent — and they
        are what fills most tins on most shelves.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>The gardens</h2>
    <p class="gardens-intro">
      Four gardens across three regions, every harvest kept separate. Poured side by side, they are not subtly different
      — and which one suits you tends to depend on the time of day more than anything else.
    </p>
    <div class="gardens">
      {gardens.map((garden) => (
        <div>
          <h3 class="eyebrow">{garden.name}</h3>
          <p>{garden.text}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="more"><a href="/why-origin-matters/">More on why origin matters →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="block last">
    <h2>Milling</h2>
    <p>
      Matcha is ground between granite wheels turning slowly enough to produce thirty to forty grams in an hour. A single
      100g bag is most of a working day.
    </p>
    <p>
      The slowness is not ceremony. Friction makes heat, and heat destroys the volatile compounds that carry aroma. A fast
      mill produces powder of roughly the right colour that tastes of comparatively little. There is no shortcut here that
      survives tasting.
    </p>
    <hr />
    <h2>What we believe</h2>
    <p>
      Matcha is perishable in a way most people are never told. It begins losing aroma the moment it is milled, and once
      a bag is opened it has perhaps four to six weeks before the colour dulls and the sweetness goes with it.
    </p>
    <p>
      So we buy in small quantities, hold little stock, and ship within weeks of harvest rather than months. We would
      rather sell out of something than sell it tired.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some years a garden gives us a remarkable tea. Some years it gives us a merely good one. We could smooth that out by
      blending. We would rather tell you which year you are drinking.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button" href="/product-category/single-origin/">Shop Single Origin</a>
      <a class="button ghost" href="/journal/">Read the Journal</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  const intro = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.intro')!;
  const canvas = intro.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('.dust')!;
  const motionOK = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)').matches;

  // Cursor position over the intro, so the dust can move away from it.
  const pointer = { x: -9999, y: -9999 };
  if (motionOK) {
    intro.addEventListener('pointermove', (event) => {
      const r = intro.getBoundingClientRect();
      pointer.x = event.clientX - r.left;
      pointer.y = event.clientY - r.top;
    });
    intro.addEventListener('pointerleave', () => {
      pointer.x = pointer.y = -9999;
    });
  }

  // Matcha dust: fine particles drifting up, pushed gently away from the cursor.
  if (motionOK) {
    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d')!;
    const dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio, 2);
    let width = 0;
    let height = 0;
    const resize = () => {
      width = canvas.clientWidth;
      height = canvas.clientHeight;
      canvas.width = width * dpr; // sharp on high-density screens
      canvas.height = height * dpr;
      ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
    };
    resize();
    window.addEventListener('resize', resize);

    const particles = Array.from({ length: 70 }, () => ({
      x: Math.random() * width,
      y: Math.random() * height,
      radius: 0.6 + Math.random() * 1.8,
      speed: 0.15 + Math.random() * 0.35,
      drift: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.15,
      alpha: 0.15 + Math.random() * 0.35,
    }));

    let visible = false;
    let running = false;
    const tick = () => {
      if (!visible) {
        running = false; // stop drawing while off-screen
        return;
      }
      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, width, height);
      ctx.fillStyle = '#4a5d3a';
      for (const p of particles) {
        const dx = p.x - pointer.x;
        const dy = p.y - pointer.y;
        const distance = Math.hypot(dx, dy);
        if (distance < 100) {
          const push = (1 - distance / 100) * 1.5;
          p.x += (dx / (distance || 1)) * push;
          p.y += (dy / (distance || 1)) * push;
        }
        p.x += p.drift;
        p.y -= p.speed;
        if (p.y < -5) {
          p.y = height + 5;
          p.x = Math.random() * width;
        }
        if (p.x < -5) p.x = width + 5;
        if (p.x > width + 5) p.x = -5;
        ctx.globalAlpha = p.alpha;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(p.x, p.y, p.radius, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.fill();
      }
      requestAnimationFrame(tick);
    };
    new IntersectionObserver(([entry]) => {
      visible = entry.isIntersecting;
      if (visible && !running) {
        running = true;
        requestAnimationFrame(tick);
      }
    }).observe(canvas);
  }
</script>

<style>
  section {
    padding-inline: 24px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3.6vw, 38px);
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 22px;
  }
  p {
    font-size: clamp(14px, 0.875rem + ((1vw - 3.2px) * 0.234), 17px);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--color-matcha);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .hero {
    max-width: 748px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding-block: clamp(80px, 10vw, 140px) clamp(56px, 7vw, 88px);
    text-align: center;
  }
  .hero .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 22px;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(38px, 5.5vw, 62px);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: clamp(14px, 0.875rem + ((1vw - 3.2px) * 0.391), 19px);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin: 0;
  }
  /* Layering. The stack bounds the sticky intro, so it un-pins once the photo has covered it. */
  .stack {
    position: relative;
  }
  .intro {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    background: var(--color-paper);
  }
  /* margin: auto centres the hero in the screen; it sits above the dust. */
  .intro {
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .intro .hero {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    margin: auto;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .runway {
    height: 70svh;
  }

  /* Two-beat headline: each line rises inside its own clipping window. */
  .line {
    display: block;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding-bottom: 0.12em;
    margin-bottom: -0.12em;
  }
  .line > span {
    display: inline-block;
  }

  /* Dust canvas fills the intro, behind the text. */
  .dust {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .hero .eyebrow {
      animation: fade-up 0.9s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.7, 0.2, 1) 0.1s both;
    }
    .line > span {
      animation: rise 1s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.7, 0.2, 1) 0.3s both;
    }
    /* The second beat starts later and moves more slowly: "hurried" isn't. */
    .line.slow > span {
      animation-duration: 1.8s;
      animation-delay: 1.2s;
    }
    .lead {
      animation: fade-up 1s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.7, 0.2, 1) 2.2s both;
    }
  }
  @keyframes rise {
    from {
      transform: translateY(110%);
    }
  }
  @keyframes fade-up {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(14px);
    }
  }

  /* Scroll-read: while the runway passes, each word goes from pale to full ink in turn.
     timeline-scope lets the paragraph follow the runway's progress although it isn't inside it. */
  @supports (timeline-scope: --read) {
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
      .stack {
        timeline-scope: --read;
      }
      .runway {
        view-timeline-name: --read;
      }
      .lead .w {
        animation-name: read;
        animation-timing-function: linear;
        animation-fill-mode: both;
        animation-timeline: --read;
        animation-range-start: entry calc(var(--i) / var(--n) * 80%);
        animation-range-end: entry calc(var(--i) / var(--n) * 80% + 20%);
      }
    }
  }
  @keyframes read {
    from {
      opacity: 0.2;
    }
  }

  /* Higher layer than the intro and Origins, with a soft shadow so it reads as on top. */
  .wide-wrap {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    box-shadow: 0 0 60px rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.18);
  }
  /* At least a screen tall (cropped to fit), so on phones it still fully covers the
     intro and hides Origins while it is tucked underneath. */
  .wide {
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 100svh;
    object-fit: cover;
  }
  .row.first {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 0;
  }
  /* Origins starts shifted up, under the photo, and slides down into place as it scrolls in.
     Longhands on purpose: the minifier would fold animation-timeline into the shorthand. */
  @supports (animation-timeline: view()) {
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
      .row.first {
        animation-name: from-under;
        animation-timing-function: linear;
        animation-fill-mode: both;
        animation-timeline: view();
        animation-range: entry 0% entry 100%;
      }
    }
  }
  @keyframes from-under {
    from {
      transform: translateY(-35%);
    }
  }

  /* Two columns, text 55% and image 45%, as on WordPress. */
  .row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 55fr 45fr;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 64px;
    max-width: 1168px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding-block: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px);
  }
  .row.first {
    padding-top: clamp(64px, 8vw, 112px);
  }
  .row.reverse {
    grid-template-columns: 45fr 55fr;
  }
  .row :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .block {
    max-width: 1168px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding-block: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px);
  }
  .block.last {
    padding-block: clamp(48px, 6vw, 80px) clamp(72px, 9vw, 120px);
  }
  .gardens-intro {
    margin-bottom: 44px;
  }
  .gardens {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 40px;
  }
  .gardens h3 {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  .gardens p {
    font-size: clamp(14px, 0.875rem + ((1vw - 3.2px) * 0.156), 16px);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .more {
    margin-top: 44px;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .more a {
    color: var(--color-stone-strong);
  }
  hr {
    height: 1px;
    border: 0;
    background: var(--color-stone);
    margin: clamp(48px, 6vw, 72px) 0;
  }
  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 48px;
  }
  .actions .button {
    padding: 17px 38px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 781.98px) {
    .row,
    .row.reverse,
    .gardens {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .row {
      gap: 40px;
    }
    /* Text first on phones, as WordPress stacks the columns. */
    .row.reverse :global(img) {
      order: 1;
    }
  }
</style>
